          "issue": "Independently checked against the selected Greek and supplied apparatus, this note makes the same unsupported characterization: the reported Athos reading is ἀνένευσε, not an established same-meaning grammatical variant of ἀνενέωσε. Its written form belongs to ἀνανεύω, associated with nodding or a gesture of refusal. Neither the supplied transcription nor the comparison reports establish that it was intended as an orthographic corruption meaning “renewed.” The simplified main text correctly retains the working reading.",
          "suggested_revision": "Keep “he renewed our life.” Replace the inaccurate variant description with an explicit report, for example: “The working text reads ‘renewed.’ Its apparatus cites Latin Vulgata and Palatina and reports Athos ἀνένευσε, a different Greek form whose intended meaning here is uncertain. The supplied evidence does not establish that this form also means ‘renewed.’ The source separately describes renewal of our spirit and our life.” Any stronger account needs additional attributed evidence, and this proposed replacement requires fresh review.",
